            <title xml:id="title_699N2018D" xml:lang="da">Religiøse og folkelige Digte af Ad. Langsted og Ernst v. d. Recke</title>
            <title xml:id="title_eb314e2d" xml:lang="en">Religious and Folk-like Poems by Ad. Langsted and Ernst v.d. Recke</title>
            <contributor xml:id="idm115">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_699N20193">J.P.E. Hartmann</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_df2c814b">Adolf Langsted</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_879322f9">Ernst von der Recke</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_699N20198">
               <date xml:id="idm120" enddate="1888-11-12" startdate="1888-07-02">2 July to 12 Nov. 1888</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_699N20196">
               <p xml:id="idm122">In December 1887, at the request of Hartmann the poet and school master Adolf Langsted sent him some information concerning those songs in his "Et Korstog. En religiøs-romantisk Digtning" (A Crusade. A Religious-Romantic Poem), which were suited for music. It was Langsted's wish that the songs should be ready for the confirmation services in March, but Hartmann did not compose them until July-Aug. 1888. <lb xml:id="idm123"/>The six "Folkelige Digte" (Folk-like Poems) by Ernst v.d. Recke were all written in Oct.-Nov. 1888, but nothing else is known about their genesis.</p>
            </history>
